[P0] `.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W4-C-DOS-474.md:19,284` — `v280` is not safe to land ahead of lower reserved slots. The migration runner uses `MAX(version)` and only applies `version > current` (`src-tauri/src/migrations.rs:2116,3608`), so any DB that records v280 will permanently skip later v260-v279 migrations. v1.4.6 still reserves v260-v279, and PR #366 already adds v260. Action: block W4-C until all lower slots land, or coordinate a global renumber so no future migration lands below W4-C.

[P1] `.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W4-C-DOS-474.md:286` — the proposed multi-table migration is not atomic or rerun-safe under the live runner’s `execute_batch` behavior (`src-tauri/src/migrations.rs:3662`). If the process dies after the first `CREATE TABLE`, rerun can fail before `schema_version` is recorded. Action: wrap the migration in `BEGIN IMMEDIATE; ... COMMIT;` and use `IF NOT EXISTS`, or implement it as a `Migration::Fn`.

[P1] `.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W4-C-DOS-474.md:324` — service hourly rate limiting is specified as prune/count/insert, but not as an atomic reservation. The gateway’s equivalent path uses `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` around prune/count/insert (`src-tauri/src/services/mcp_v2/gateway.rs:604`). Action: require the same transaction semantics for `workspace_placement_rate_ledger` and add a concurrent 200/hour boundary test.

[P1] `.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W4-C-DOS-474.md:326,329` — placement `in_progress` rows have no stale/crash recovery path. A crash after fence acquisition can leave the key returning `idempotency_in_progress` forever, unlike `RunsRepo`, which aborts stale in-progress runs after 1 hour (`src-tauri/src/services/workspace_ingestion/runs.rs:18,188`). Action: add stale reconciliation for placement rows, including orphan-file cleanup or success reconstruction.

[P1] `.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W4-C-DOS-474.md:114,324` — `allowed_modes = [Live, Simulate, Evaluate]` conflicts with the plan’s live service-ledger writes. The runtime permits invocation by mode first (`src-tauri/abilities-runtime/src/abilities/registry.rs:1484`), but service writes are forbidden outside Live (`src-tauri/abilities-runtime/src/services/context.rs:87,2143`). Action: either make the ability Live-only, or specify a separate non-Live dry-run path that writes no gateway/service ledgers.

[P2] `.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W4-C-DOS-474.md:246,249,337` — PR #355 changes the MCP handler seam, but the packet does not freeze a branch-order implementation path. PR #355 introduces `McpHandlerContext` in the handler trait and a CI gate banning direct DB opens in handlers. Action: add a conditional: if #355 lands first, `tool_placement.rs` must implement the new context signature and satisfy that gate; if W4-C lands first, #355 owns the rebase.

Final verdict: HOLD.